95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add named RED-first tests for the fingerprint-MISMATCH degraded path (falls back to empty lists) and the contradictory-stored-verdict path (BLOCK stored + attestation valid → do not replay blocking findings), alongside the unreadable fail-open test.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope 1: 'when it is usable and corresponds to the same material fingerprint, populate ... rather than empties' and 'if the stored sidecar verdict contradicts (BLOCK stored but attestation valid), prefer current behavior and do not replay contradictory findings.'","Scope 4 tests enumerated: 'a reuse-path test proving stored advisory/coaching are replayed on PASS reuse', 'a fail-open test (sidecar unreadable → reuse still fires with empty lists)', 'a rendering test for the notation.' — no test named for fingerprint-mismatch degradation or contradictory-verdict suppression."],"finding":"Scope item 1 introduces three distinct degraded/branching behaviors for PASS reuse — (a) sidecar unreadable/absent, (b) sidecar present but material-fingerprint MISMATCH, (c) sidecar present but its stored verdict CONTRADICTS the valid attestation (BLOCK stored) — but the enumerated tests in scope item 4 name a test only for the unreadable/fail-open case. The fingerprint-mismatch degraded path and the contradiction-suppression path are new conditional branches with no named test coverage.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3a29f6c5be5c49b4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope items 1 and 4; AC line 'PASS reuse replays ... when the sidecar matches the current material fingerprint; degraded empty-list behavior preserved when it does not.'","norm_id":"n25af2e4f14a75db2","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future refactor of the fingerprint-match guard silently regresses to replaying findings from a sidecar that does not match the current material, and no test catches it.","The contradiction guard (BLOCK stored, attestation valid) is dropped and stale blocking findings leak into a PASS reuse render, with no test asserting the suppression."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In scope item 4, extend the enumerated test list with (1) a mismatched-fingerprint sidecar test asserting empty-list degradation on PASS reuse, and (2) a contradictory-verdict test asserting stored BLOCK findings are NOT replayed when the attestation is valid.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the PASS-reuse path reconstructs `indeterminate` from the flattened stored `findings` list (name the decision-key/attribute that selects indeterminate findings, or state explicitly that indeterminate stays empty and why), given SURFACED_DECISIONS has no 'indeterminate' member.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decisi